From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: A733 eMMC - program the card threshold and the FIFO watermark

Every HS400 hypothesis so far has been a phase or a delay. This one is neither,
and it is the first candidate in this series that touches a register the driver
has never written at all.

SMHC_THLD (0x100) resets to 0x5: CARD_WR_THLD_ENB and CARD_RD_THLD_ENB both SET,
with a threshold size of 0. sunxi-mmc.c never writes that register, so we run
with both gates armed and both trivially satisfied. What the UM
says about the two enables makes that a defect rather than a default:

    CARD_WR_THLD_ENB  a write transfer starts only once the transmit FIFO holds
                      at least the card-threshold amount of data
    CARD_RD_THLD_ENB  a read transfer starts only once the receive FIFO has at
                      least CARD_RD_THLD of free space

With the size at 0 both conditions hold before a single byte has moved. The
protection is not disabled, it is vacuous - which is why nothing has ever
reported it.

SMHC_SFC (0x104) says what the mechanism is for: when the read threshold equals
BLK_SZ (CARD_RD_THLD_ENB set), the controller may pause the card clock between
blocks on a read. The block gap is where a stall is legal. Without a
threshold the controller can only stall inside a block, and in HS400 - 8-bit DDR
framed by the card's own strobe - an in-block stall is a framing error by
construction. That is the error class we measure: cmd 25 WR DCE / WR DCE EBE and
cmd 18 RD DCE SBE, CRC together with start- and end-bit errors, in both
directions.

The transmit trigger level is the other half of the same mechanism. We write
SMHC_FIFOTH = 0x20070008 (burst 8, RX_TL 7, TX_TL 8), so transmission may start
with 32 bytes buffered against a 512-byte block. The UM recommends burst 16,
TX_TL 240, RX_TL 15 for this controller (11.3.8.17 - the only two occurrences of
"recommend" in ch. 11.3 are about this register) and its single-block-write
procedure (11.3.6.2) writes the literal value 0x300F00F0. Vendor silicon on the 8 GiB board
reads exactly 0x300f00f0 while writing this eMMC at HS400.

Measured on that board on 2026-07-25, in the vendor's working HS400 state, by
writing 64 MiB and then reading it back and reading SMHC_THLD after each:

    after the write:  0x02000004    size 512, write gate on,  read gate off
    after the read:   0x02000001    size 512, write gate off, read gate on
    SMHC_FIFOTH:      0x300f00f0    unchanged in both

The per-transfer switching this patch implements is therefore measured on
silicon in both directions, not inferred from vendor source.

So the two are one setting, not two knobs: the write gate waits for a whole
block in the FIFO, and only a transmit trigger level that can hold a whole block
lets that condition ever come true. Enabling either alone does nothing - which is
also why an earlier conclusion (2026-07-24), that FIFOTH is a real defect but not this bug, does not
settle it. That conclusion rested on the absence of FIFO_RUN_ERROR, and FE is the
controller reporting its own FIFO misuse, not the threshold mechanism; the UM
treats them in separate paragraphs. The live FIFOTH test planned for that same
boot ("set it via devmem and write again") has no recorded result - it never ran.
SMHC_THLD was never examined at all.

It also fits the asymmetry none of the timing hypotheses explained: HS200 at the
same 150 MHz is error-free while HS400 fails. HS400 is DDR, so it moves twice the
bytes per clock through the same FIFO with the same watermarks.

Implementation:

- fifoth becomes a cfg field. Unset means the historic 0x20070008, so no other
  SoC changes behaviour; the A733 eMMC gets 0x300f00f0.
- sunxi_mmc_set_thld() programs SMHC_THLD per transfer from data->blksz and
  enables the gate for the direction in flight. The guards are the physical ones
  (a threshold larger than the FIFO can never be reached), mirroring the vendor's
  conditions.

Not gated on HS400: the mechanism is a property of the data path, the vendor
programs it in every mode, and the same guards keep it inert where a block does
not fit. The SD controller keeps the old watermark and is unaffected in every
mode by construction.

HYPOTHESIS, NOT PROVEN. Compile-clean (aarch64, W=1) and mechanism-complete, but
no board has run it. The measurement that decides it is the error-class
histogram: it empties out or it does not.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -71,12 +71,13 @@
 #define SDXC_REG_A12A		0x058 /* SMC Auto Command 12 Register */
 #define SDXC_REG_SD_NTSR	0x05C /* SMC New Timing Set Register */
 #define SDXC_REG_DRV_DL		0x140 /* Drive Delay Control Register */
 #define SDXC_REG_SAMP_DL_REG	0x144 /* SMC sample delay control */
 #define SDXC_REG_DS_DL_REG	0x148 /* SMC data strobe delay control */
 #define SDXC_REG_CSDC		0x054 /* CRC Status Detect Control (HS400) */
+#define SDXC_REG_THLD		0x100 /* Card Threshold Control */
 #define SDXC_REG_EMMC_DSBD	0x10C /* eMMC DDR Start Bit Detect Control */
 
 /* HS400 data-strobe fields (A733 UM 11.3, V5P3X controller) */
 #define SDXC_HS400_MD_EN		BIT(31)	  /* EMMC_DSBD: HS400 mode enable */
 #define SDXC_HALF_START_BIT		BIT(0)	  /* EMMC_DSBD: half start-bit (eMMC>=4.5) */
 #define SDXC_HS400_NEW_SAM_EN		BIT(0)	  /* SD_NTSR: HS400 new sample */
@@ -85,12 +86,26 @@
 #define SDXC_NTSR_DAT_SAM_PH_HS400	(0x3 << 8) /* SD2 HS400: 0 degree */
 #define SDXC_CSDC_CRC_DET_MASK		0xf
 #define SDXC_CSDC_HS400			0x6	  /* CSDC: HS400 speed mode */
 #define SDXC_CSDC_OTHER			0x3	  /* CSDC: non-HS400 speed mode */
 #define SDXC_DS_DL_SW_MASK		0x3f	  /* DS_DL: 6-bit SW delay */
 
+/* SMHC_THLD (UM 11.3.8.29). Reset value is 0x5: both gates ENABLED with a
+ * threshold size of 0, i.e. armed and vacuous -- see sunxi_mmc_set_thld(). */
+#define SDXC_CARD_THLD_SIZE_MASK	GENMASK(28, 16)
+#define SDXC_CARD_THLD_SIZE_SHIFT	16
+#define SDXC_CARD_THLD_SIZE_MAX		0x1fff
+#define SDXC_CARD_WR_THLD_ENB		BIT(2)
+#define SDXC_CARD_RD_THLD_ENB		BIT(0)
+
+/* FIFO geometry, UM 11.3.8.17: FIFO_DEPTH = 256 words = 1 KiB. */
+#define SDXC_FIFO_BYTES			1024
+/* Burst 8, RX trigger level 7, TX trigger level 8 -- the value this driver has
+ * always written. Kept as the default so no existing SoC changes behaviour. */
+#define SDXC_FIFOTH_DEFAULT		0x20070008
+
 #define mmc_readl(host, reg) \
 	readl((host)->reg_base + SDXC_##reg)
 #define mmc_writel(host, reg, value) \
 	writel((value), (host)->reg_base + SDXC_##reg)
 
 /* global control register bits */
@@ -278,12 +293,15 @@ struct sunxi_mmc_cfg {
 
 	/* clock hardware can switch between old and new timing modes */
 	bool ccu_has_timings_switch;
 
 	/* controller carries the HS400 data-strobe delay path */
 	bool can_hs400;
+
+	/* SMHC_FIFOTH value; 0 selects SDXC_FIFOTH_DEFAULT */
+	u32 fifoth;
 };
 
 struct sunxi_mmc_host {
 	struct device *dev;
 	struct mmc_host	*mmc;
 	struct reset_control *reset;
@@ -347,17 +365,25 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_init_host(struct sunxi_mmc_host *host)
 	u32 rval;
 
 	if (sunxi_mmc_reset_host(host))
 		return -EIO;
 
 	/*
-	 * Burst 8 transfers, RX trigger level: 7, TX trigger level: 8
+	 * FIFO burst size and trigger levels. The historic value is burst 8,
+	 * RX trigger 7, TX trigger 8; a cfg may override it, because the
+	 * transmit trigger level is what decides how much of a block is
+	 * buffered before the controller starts driving data at the card, and
+	 * 8 words is 32 bytes against a 512-byte block. The A733 UM recommends
+	 * burst 16 / TX 240 / RX 15 for this controller and names the literal
+	 * value 0x300F00F0 in its own single-block-write procedure (11.3.8.17,
+	 * 11.3.6.2), which is also what the vendor stack runs on silicon.
 	 *
 	 * TODO: sun9i has a larger FIFO and supports higher trigger values
 	 */
-	mmc_writel(host, REG_FTRGL, 0x20070008);
+	mmc_writel(host, REG_FTRGL,
+		   host->cfg->fifoth ? host->cfg->fifoth : SDXC_FIFOTH_DEFAULT);
 	/* Maximum timeout value */
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_TMOUT, 0xffffffff);
 	/* Unmask SDIO interrupt if needed */
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_IMASK, host->sdio_imask);
 	/* Clear all pending interrupts */
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_RINTR, 0xffffffff);
@@ -1171,12 +1197,65 @@ static void sunxi_mmc_hw_reset(struct mmc_host *mmc)
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_HWRST, 0);
 	udelay(10);
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_HWRST, 1);
 	udelay(300);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Card read/write threshold (SMHC_THLD, UM 11.3.8.29).
+ *
+ * The register resets to 0x5 -- CARD_WR_THLD_ENB and CARD_RD_THLD_ENB both set
+ * with a threshold size of 0. A driver that never writes it therefore runs with
+ * both gates armed and both trivially satisfied ("start the transfer once 0
+ * bytes are available"), which is not the same as having no flow control: it is
+ * flow control that never engages, and nothing reports it.
+ *
+ * What the gates are for, per the UM: a write transfer starts only once the
+ * transmit FIFO holds the card-threshold amount of data, and a read transfer
+ * only once the receive FIFO has CARD_RD_THLD of free space. SMHC_SFC adds
+ * the reason it matters here -- a read threshold equal to the block size
+ * lets the controller pause the card clock between blocks on a read.
+ * Block gap is where a stall is legal. Without the
+ * threshold the controller can only stall inside a block, and in HS400 (8-bit
+ * DDR framed by the card's strobe) an in-block stall is a framing error.
+ *
+ * So: program the size to the block size, and enable the gate for the direction
+ * actually in flight. The guards mirror the vendor's, whose conditions are the
+ * physical ones -- a threshold larger than the FIFO can never be reached.
+ */
+static void sunxi_mmc_set_thld(struct sunxi_mmc_host *host,
+			       struct mmc_data *data)
+{
+	u32 fifoth = host->cfg->fifoth ? host->cfg->fifoth : SDXC_FIFOTH_DEFAULT;
+	u32 tx_bytes = (fifoth & 0xff) * 4;
+	u32 rx_bytes = ((fifoth >> 16) & 0x7ff) * 4;
+	u32 rval;
+
+	rval = mmc_readl(host, REG_THLD);
+	rval &= ~(SDXC_CARD_THLD_SIZE_MASK | SDXC_CARD_WR_THLD_ENB |
+		  SDXC_CARD_RD_THLD_ENB);
+
+	if (data->blksz <= SDXC_CARD_THLD_SIZE_MAX) {
+		if (data->flags & MMC_DATA_WRITE) {
+			/*
+			 * The transmit trigger level must be able to hold a
+			 * whole block, or the gate would wait for data the
+			 * FIFO is never allowed to accumulate.
+			 */
+			if (data->blksz <= tx_bytes)
+				rval |= (data->blksz << SDXC_CARD_THLD_SIZE_SHIFT) |
+					SDXC_CARD_WR_THLD_ENB;
+		} else if (rx_bytes + data->blksz <= SDXC_FIFO_BYTES) {
+			rval |= (data->blksz << SDXC_CARD_THLD_SIZE_SHIFT) |
+				SDXC_CARD_RD_THLD_ENB;
+		}
+	}
+
+	mmc_writel(host, REG_THLD, rval);
+}
+
 static void sunxi_mmc_request(struct mmc_host *mmc, struct mmc_request *mrq)
 {
 	struct sunxi_mmc_host *host = mmc_priv(mmc);
 	struct mmc_command *cmd = mrq->cmd;
 	struct mmc_data *data = mrq->data;
 	unsigned long iflags;
@@ -1255,12 +1334,13 @@ static void sunxi_mmc_request(struct mmc_host *mmc, struct mmc_request *mrq)
 		return;
 	}
 
 	if (data) {
 		mmc_writel(host, REG_BLKSZ, data->blksz);
 		mmc_writel(host, REG_BCNTR, data->blksz * data->blocks);
+		sunxi_mmc_set_thld(host, data);
 		sunxi_mmc_start_dma(host, data);
 	}
 
 	host->mrq = mrq;
 	host->wait_dma = wait_dma;
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_IMASK, host->sdio_imask | imask);
@@ -1379,12 +1459,18 @@ static const struct sunxi_mmc_cfg sun60i_a733_emmc_cfg = {
 	.idma_des_size_bits = 13,
 	.idma_des_shift = 2,
 	.can_calibrate = true,
 	.mask_data0 = true,
 	.needs_new_timings = true,
 	.can_hs400 = true,
+	/* UM 11.3.8.17 recommends BSIZE_OF_TRANS = 3 (MSize 16), TX_TL = 240
+	 * and RX_TL = 15, and 11.3.6.2 writes 0x300F00F0 verbatim.
+	 * Vendor silicon on the 8 GiB board reads exactly this while writing this eMMC
+	 * at HS400.
+	 */
+	.fifoth = 0x300f00f0,
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id sunxi_mmc_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun4i-a10-mmc", .data = &sun4i_a10_cfg },
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun5i-a13-mmc", .data = &sun5i_a13_cfg },
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun7i-a20-mmc", .data = &sun7i_a20_cfg },
